msgctxt "#31540"
msgid "Dark is the listening room at night: the art is the only light. Light is a warm paper room with dark ink; the art casts its colour onto the page. Playback over video and the visualiser stay dark in both."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31541"
msgid "With disc art, the record that slides out of the sleeve is the album's own printed disc. Always vinyl draws a black record with the cover as its label for every album."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31542"
msgid "How strongly the focused art colours the room around it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31543"
msgid "Record opens Now Playing on the spinning record every time. Last used remembers whether you left it on the record or the visualiser."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31544"
msgid "The small disc in the corner while music plays. Still keeps it without turning; Off hides it (Now Playing stays one press away from Home)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31545"
msgid "Slides, tilts and spins become instant changes; the record and the mini disc stand still. Fades stay."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31546"
msgid "Films and shows (and albums, where it can) take their glow from TMDb Helper's colour service. Off uses the art's own soft light instead."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31547"
msgid "The controls over a playing film fade away after this long without a key press (never while paused)."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31548"
msgid "Every Groove setting goes back to how it was built: Dark room, disc art, medium glow, Now Playing on the record, spinning mini player, full motion, TMDb colours on, controls hiding after five seconds."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31549"
msgid "An optional helper shared by KarmaMole's skins. In Vernissage it makes the black-and-white prints, fills Still on the easel and New in the collection, tints the spotlight with the art and shuffles albums. Vernissage works without it. Kodi installs it from KarmaMole's repository."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#31550"
msgid "Gives the Shadertoy visualisers the colours of the playing album's cover, and Now Playing's glow when the KarmaMole Skin Helper isn't there. Kodi installs it from KarmaMole's repository."
msgstr ""

